From: richie-rich90454 <rjiang880@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0005/0014] Remove AI features

This patch removes the GitHub Copilot surfaces from the workbench:
the default chat participant view is renamed from the hardcoded
'GitHub Copilot' to 'Chat', and the Copilot compatibility notifier
(which only ever handled the github.copilot-chat extension) is
removed with its registration. The chat framework itself stays so a
user-installed provider from Open VSX keeps working; with no provider
installed no chat UI appears, exactly as in stock OSS.

The OSS tree ships no Copilot, chat-model, or prompt-tsx code to
remove: github.copilot-chat is a marketplace extension, and
@vscode/prompt-tsx is not a dependency of this tree.

Rationale: no AI feature ships in the IDE. Users may install an
extension from Open VSX; none is shipped or endorsed.

Touches:
  - workbench chat participant view name
  - Copilot compatibility notifier (removed with registration)

Verification: patch regression test fails without it and passes with it.

---
